<article class="env-lemma" id="04QE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04QE">Lemma <span data-tag="04QE">79.12.8</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Suppose that $U$ is a scheme, $U \to Y$ is an étale morphism and $Z \subset U \times _ Y X$ is an open subspace finite over $U$. Then the induced morphism $U \to (X/Y)_{fin}$ is étale. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is formal from the description of the diagonal in Lemma <a href="/tag/04PK" data-tag="04PK">79.12.7</a> but we write it out since it is an important step in the development of the theory. We have to check that for any scheme $T$ over $S$ and a morphism $T \to (X/Y)_{fin}$ the projection map 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  T \times _{(X/Y)_{fin}} U \longrightarrow T  \]
</div>
    <p>
       is étale. Note that 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  T \times _{(X/Y)_{fin}} U = (X/Y)_{fin} \times _{((X/Y)_{fin} \times _ Y (X/Y)_{fin})} (T \times _ Y U)  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Applying the result of Lemma <a href="/tag/04PK" data-tag="04PK">79.12.7</a> we see that $T \times _{(X/Y)_{fin}} U$ is represented by an open subscheme of $T \times _ Y U$. As the projection $T \times _ Y U \to T$ is étale by Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/0466" data-tag="0466">67.39.4</a> we conclude. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>